{title: Silent Night}
{title_ko: 고요한 밤 거룩한 밤}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 109장}
{artist: Joseph Mohr / Franz Gruber}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Meditative}
{style: Carol}
{key: C}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 66}
{time: 3/4}
{score: silent-night.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Silent night, [G]holy night
[G7]All is calm, [C]all is bright
Round yon [F]virgin, mother and [C]child
Holy infant so [F]tender and [C]mild
Sleep in heavenly [G]peace
Sleep in heavenly [C]peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Silent night, [G]holy night
[G7]Shepherds quake [C]at the sight
Glories [F]stream from heaven a[C]far
Heavenly hosts sing [F]Alle[C]luia
Christ the Saviour is [G]born
Christ the Saviour is [C]born
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Silent night, [G]holy night
[G7]Son of God, [C]love's pure light
Radiant [F]beams from thy holy [C]face
With the dawn of re[F]deeming [C]grace
Jesus, Lord, at thy [G]birth
Jesus, Lord, at thy [C]birth
{end_of_verse}
